DeepResearch Bench — vendored components
========================================

This directory contains material redistributed from the DeepResearch Bench
project, used here as the frozen external holdout for the deep-research
measurement work (see ../README.md "Provenance").

  Upstream:  https://github.com/Ayanami0730/deep_research_bench
  Commit:    469cce54ea7f6a63c163d3d9fec879cf289ec484 (2026-05-11)
  Paper:     arXiv 2506.11763 v2, Appendix E
  License:   Apache License 2.0 (full text in ./LICENSE)

Redistributed here
------------------

  utils/                     the official FACT pipeline (extract, deduplicate,
                             validate, stat, io_utils, json_extractor,
                             score_calculator, clean_article, generate_criteria,
                             scrape) — verbatim except as noted below.

  ../leaderboard.csv         the official leaderboard, fetched verbatim
                             2026-08-16 from
                             https://huggingface.co/spaces/muset-ai/DeepResearch-Bench-Leaderboard/raw/main/data/leaderboard.csv

  ../query.full.jsonl        the upstream 100-task prompt set.
  ../query.subset.jsonl      a 10-task subset of the above, selected by the
                             content-blind seeded draw recorded in ../README.md.

  fixture-validated.jsonl    the upstream claude-3-7-sonnet-latest validated
                             output, used as the stat.py reproduction fixture.
                             NOT redistributed in this repository — it is
                             gitignored on size (69.7 MB) and is re-fetchable
                             from the pinned upstream commit above.

Modifications
-------------

Apache-2.0 §4(b) requires that modified files carry prominent notice of the
change. One file is modified:

  utils/api.py               rewritten as a drop-in replacement for the
                             upstream google.genai-backed client, exposing the
                             same surface (AIClient, call_model, scrape_url,
                             Model, FACT_Model) over an OpenAI-compatible
                             endpoint, so FACT judging can run against a local
                             daemon rather than a hosted API.

All other vendored files are unmodified. ../SHA256SUMS records the hashes the
freeze discipline re-checks at landing.
